 {"id": "coding", "keys": ["programming", "programing", "coder", "code", "coding", "developer", "development", "codex", "claude code", "clock code", "engineering", "can you build", "technical skills", "languages", "html", "javascript", "css"], "text": "Yes, I code now. I use Codex and Claude Code to turn design ideas into working browser experiences. This portfolio was built that way, including its motion and interactive demos. My foundation is product design; coding gives me another way to make the details real instead of leaving everything in a mockup.", "sources": ["portfolio"], "next": ["website", "ai-workflow", "motion"]},
 {"id": "website", "keys": ["this website", "this site", "your website", "your site", "portfolio website", "built this", "made this", "build this site"], "text": "This website is part portfolio, part design playground. I built it with AI-assisted coding, using Codex and Claude Code. The moving cards, case-study sheets, playful typography, and interactive app demos let me explore the gap between designing something and making it feel right in a browser.", "sources": ["portfolio"], "next": ["coding", "motion", "ai-workflow"]},
 {"id": "ai-workflow", "keys": ["ai workflow", "ai coding", "vibe coding", "use ai", "using ai", "artificial intelligence", "ai replace", "ai does everything", "ai wrote", "prompting"], "text": "I use Codex and Claude Code as tools for building and iterating. They don’t make taste decisions for me. I still have to decide what the experience should do, judge what feels wrong, and keep refining it. Coding with AI makes it easier to try a direction in the browser and see whether the design actually holds up.", "sources": ["portfolio"], "next": ["coding", "iteration", "craft"]},
 {"id": "working-style", "keys": ["working with you", "work with you", "work together", "working style", "teammate", "personality", "easy to work with", "scrappy", "team player", "fun to work with"], "text": "Scrappy ideas to polished craft is a pretty good description of how I like to work. I want to move quickly enough to learn something, then give the details the attention they deserve. I care about making ideas tangible and being easy to work with. A useful prototype beats a very long explanation.", "sources": ["portfolio"], "next": ["iteration", "approach", "coding"]},
 {"id": "iteration", "keys": ["iteration", "iterate", "iterations", "refine", "feedback loop", "improve a design", "polishing"], "text": "I’m comfortable changing direction when something isn’t working. Everkind went through many iterations before the V2 shown here, and this portfolio has been a continuous exercise in trying things, spotting the awkward bits, and refining them. The first version is a way to learn, not something to defend forever.", "sources": ["portfolio"], "next": ["everkind-process", "craft", "website"]},
 {"id": "motion", "keys": ["motion", "animation", "animations", "interaction", "microinteraction", "microinteractions", "transitions", "shuffle", "shuffling", "gooey"], "text": "I like motion that gives an interface character and makes its behaviour easier to follow. On this site, cards shuffle, case studies open as sheets, and the typography has playful interactions. Making those ideas work in the browser also means paying attention to timing, mobile behaviour, and performance. A fun effect still has to feel good to use.", "sources": ["portfolio"], "next": ["website", "coding", "craft"]},
 {"id": "skills", "keys": ["skills", "skill set", "skillset", "what can you do", "capabilities", "specialty", "specialties", "what do you bring", "what are you good at"], "text": "I connect product design, visual craft, design systems, prototyping, and now AI-assisted coding. I’ve designed across SaaS, apps, and websites. That means I can work on the structure of an experience, get into the interface details, and build ideas to see how they behave. I’m a product designer with a growing ability to bring the work to life in code.", "sources": ["portfolio"], "next": ["coding", "systems", "craft"]},
 {"id": "platforms", "keys": ["saas", "mobile apps", "app design", "web design", "websites", "platforms", "desktop", "responsive"], "text": "I work across SaaS, apps, and websites rather than treating them as the same problem in different sizes. Everkind is an app experience built around conversation and reflection; Melon makes booking choices clearer; RISD translates an institution’s identity into a website. The medium changes, but I keep coming back to clarity, hierarchy, and craft.", "sources": ["portfolio"], "next": ["everkind", "trains", "risd"]},
 {"id": "ownership", "keys": ["your contribution", "your role", "what did you do", "what did you design", "responsibility", "responsibilities", "ownership", "own work"], "text": "I’m a product designer, and the contribution depends on the project. For Everkind, I designed the first vision and developed it through iterations into V2. For Melon Trains, I redesigned how people compare a journey. For RISD, I designed the new identity’s digital expression across the homepage, Student Hub, and faculty profiles. Those are different kinds of design work, not one process pasted onto every project.", "sources": ["portfolio"], "next": ["everkind-process", "trains-process", "risd"]},
 {"id": "learning", "keys": ["learning", "learn", "growth", "growing", "new skills", "learn to code", "learned to code", "getting better"], "text": "Coding is one of the ways I’m expanding what I can make. Codex and Claude Code let me explore working interactions alongside the visual design. I’m not swapping design for code; I’m adding another way to test and express an idea. This portfolio is a hands-on example of that.", "sources": ["portfolio"], "next": ["coding", "website", "iteration"]}
,
 {"id": "flights", "keys": ["melon flights", "melon flight search", "flight search", "flights", "flight results", "search results", "choosing a flight", "compare flights"], "text": "The Melon flight-search redesign is a desktop SaaS project about making a flight choice easier to compare. I designed the result layout so route, schedule, and price could be read together. Expanded flight details and fare information let people inspect the journey without losing the context of the results. It is separate from the train-booking case study, but part of the same travel product.", "sources": ["portfolio"], "next": ["checkout", "trains", "approach"]},
 {"id": "checkout", "keys": ["melon checkout", "checkout", "confirmation", "payment flow", "trip review", "booking confirmation", "seat selection", "loyalty"], "text": "The Melon checkout redesign takes the traveller from a selected journey to a reviewed booking and a trip they can return to. I designed around traveller and loyalty details, trip and seat information, company-policy requirements, payment, and a final review. The idea was to give each part a clear place instead of making the whole checkout feel like one dense task.", "sources": ["portfolio"], "next": ["flights", "trains", "approach"]},
 {"id": "qatar", "keys": ["qatar", "qatar 2022", "fifa", "world cup", "sc qa", "hospitality", "tournament"], "text": "I worked with SC.qa at Zoocha ahead of the 2022 World Cup on a hospitality website for visitors to Qatar. This was client work, not a personal concept. I worked with the official tournament branding and destination content, bringing the anticipation of the event together with practical trip planning. Typography, colour, photography, and the structure of the content all helped introduce the place as well as the tournament.", "sources": ["portfolio", "linkedin"], "next": ["history", "craft", "georgia"]},
 {"id": "absorb-workflow", "keys": ["absorb workflow", "absorb coding", "code at absorb", "coding at absorb", "ai at absorb", "absorb ai", "absorb features", "new features", "shape features", "shaping features", "current responsibilities"], "text": "At Absorb, I’m working as a designer who codes as well. I help product shape new features, using AI to support the work and make ideas more tangible. That means I can contribute to the design direction and explore how an interaction actually behaves, rather than only describing it in a static screen. My role connects product thinking, interface craft, and building.", "sources": ["portfolio"], "next": ["current", "coding", "approach"]}
